IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc2-piracy-air-sea.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II, ss 74 to 78.1 ("Piracy", "Offences against Air or Maritime Safety"): piracy, piratical acts, hijacking,
-- endangering the safety of an aircraft or airport, weapons and explosives on board a civil aircraft, ships and fixed platforms.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) / NOTHING (not covered): see the header of ccc2-treason.l4 and NOTES.md.

§ `Section 74 -- Piracy by law of nations`

-- Subsection (1): "Every one commits piracy who does any act that, by the law of nations, is piracy." The law of nations is outside the sources: its answer is a seam input.
-- src:1134 | Piracy by law of nations
-- src:1135 | 74 (1) Every one commits piracy who does any act that, by the law of nations, is piracy.
@ref Criminal Code s 74(1) (piracy by law of nations) (src:1134-1135)
GIVEN `the act is piracy by the law of nations` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1) the person commits piracy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the act is piracy by the law of nations`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any act that, by the law of nations, is piracy" (the question is handed to the law of nations, which says no)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the law of nations is not among the sources

-- Subsection (2): "Every one who commits piracy while in or out of Canada is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life." No limit of place.
-- src:1136 | Punishment
-- src:1137 | (2) Every one who commits piracy while in or out of Canada is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 74(2) (punishment) (src:1136-1137)
GIVEN `s 74(1) the person commits piracy: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(2) the person who commits piracy is guilty` MEANS `s 74(1) the person commits piracy: the answer`   -- the answer of subsection (1), in or out of Canada

@ref Criminal Code s 74(2) (punishment) (src:1136-1137)
`s 74(2) the class of the offence of piracy` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 74(2) (punishment) (src:1136-1137)
`s 74(2) the punishment for piracy` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 75 -- Piratical acts`

-- src:1138 | Piratical acts
-- src:1139 | 75 Every one who, while in or out of Canada,
-- src:1140 | (a) steals a Canadian ship,
-- src:1141 | (b) steals or without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Canadian ship,
-- src:1142 | (c) does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Canadian ship, or
-- src:1143 | (d) counsels a person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c),
-- src:1144 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 75 (piratical acts) (src:1138-1144)
DECLARE `s 75 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 75(a) steals a Canadian ship`
    `s 75(b) steals anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Canadian ship`
    `s 75(b) without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Canadian ship`
    `s 75(c) does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Canadian ship`
    `s 75(d) counsels a person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
    `s 75 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)`

-- "steals or without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys": "without lawful authority" is read as qualifying throwing overboard, damaging and destroying only (fork F13).
@ref Criminal Code s 75 (piratical acts) (src:1138-1144)
GIVEN act IS A `s 75 act`
      `the ship is a Canadian ship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75 the person commits a piratical act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `s 75 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one who, while in or out of Canada, (a) ... (d)"
        IF NOT `the ship is a Canadian ship` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a Canadian ship"
        IF act EQUALS `s 75(b) without lawful authority throws overboard, damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo, supplies or fittings in a Canadian ship` AND NOT `the person acts without lawful authority` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful authority"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 75 (piratical acts) (src:1138-1144)
`s 75 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 75 (piratical acts) (src:1138-1144)
`s 75 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 76 -- Hijacking`

-- src:1147 | Hijacking
-- src:1148 | 76 Every one who, unlawfully, by force or threat thereof, or by any other form of intimidation, seizes or exercises control of an aircraft with intent
-- src:1149 | (a) to cause any person on board the aircraft to be confined or imprisoned against his will,
-- src:1150 | (b) to cause any person on board the aircraft to be transported against his will to any place other than the next scheduled place of landing of the aircraft,
-- src:1151 | (c) to hold any person on board the aircraft for ransom or to service against his will, or
-- src:1152 | (d) to cause the aircraft to deviate in a material respect from its flight plan,
-- src:1153 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 76 (hijacking) (src:1147-1153)
DECLARE `s 76 intent` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(a) to cause any person on board the aircraft to be confined or imprisoned against his will`
    `s 76(b) to cause any person on board the aircraft to be transported against his will to any place other than the next scheduled place of landing of the aircraft`
    `s 76(c) to hold any person on board the aircraft for ransom or to service against his will`
    `s 76(d) to cause the aircraft to deviate in a material respect from its flight plan`
    `s 76 another intent`

@ref Criminal Code s 76 (hijacking) (src:1147-1153)
GIVEN `the person acts unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person seizes or exercises control of an aircraft by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      intent IS A `s 76 intent`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76 the person commits hijacking` MEANS
    IF `the person acts unlawfully` AND `the person seizes or exercises control of an aircraft by force or threat of force, or by any other form of intimidation` AND NOT (intent EQUALS `s 76 another intent`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, unlawfully, by force or threat thereof, or by any other form of intimidation, seizes or exercises control of an aircraft with intent (a) ... (d)"

@ref Criminal Code s 76 (hijacking) (src:1147-1153)
`s 76 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 76 (hijacking) (src:1147-1153)
`s 76 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 77 -- Endangering safety of aircraft or airport`

-- src:1154 | Endangering safety of aircraft or airport
-- src:1155 | 77 Every one who
-- src:1156 | (a) on board an aircraft in flight, commits an act of violence against a person that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft,
-- src:1157 | (b) using a weapon, commits an act of violence against a person at an airport serving international civil aviation that causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death and that endangers or is likely to endanger safety at the airport,
-- src:1158 | (c) causes damage to an aircraft in service that renders the aircraft incapable of flight or that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft in flight,
-- src:1159 | (d) places or causes to be placed on board an aircraft in service anything that is likely to cause damage to the aircraft, that will render it incapable of flight or that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft in flight,
-- src:1160 | (e) causes damage to or interferes with the operation of any air navigation facility where the damage or interference is likely to endanger the safety of an aircraft in flight,
-- src:1161 | (f) using a weapon, substance or device, destroys or causes serious damage to the facilities of an airport serving international civil aviation or to any aircraft not in service located there, or causes disruption of services of the airport, that endangers or is likely to endanger safety at the airport, or
-- src:1162 | (g) endangers the safety of an aircraft in flight by communicating to any other person any information that the person knows to be false,
-- src:1163 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 77 (endangering safety of aircraft or airport) (src:1154-1163)
DECLARE `s 77 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 77(a) on board an aircraft in flight, commits an act of violence against a person that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft`
    `s 77(b) using a weapon, commits an act of violence against a person at an airport serving international civil aviation that causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death and that endangers or is likely to endanger safety at the airport`
    `s 77(c) causes damage to an aircraft in service that renders the aircraft incapable of flight or that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft in flight`
    `s 77(d) places or causes to be placed on board an aircraft in service anything that is likely to cause damage to the aircraft, that will render it incapable of flight or that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft in flight`
    `s 77(e) causes damage to or interferes with the operation of any air navigation facility where the damage or interference is likely to endanger the safety of an aircraft in flight`
    `s 77(f) using a weapon, substance or device, destroys or causes serious damage to the facilities of an airport serving international civil aviation or to any aircraft not in service located there, or causes disruption of services of the airport, that endangers or is likely to endanger safety at the airport`
    `s 77(g) endangers the safety of an aircraft in flight by communicating to any other person any information that the person knows to be false`
    `s 77 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (g)`

-- One set of facts serves every paragraph; each branch reads only the facts its paragraph names.
@ref Criminal Code s 77 (endangering safety of aircraft or airport) (src:1154-1163)
GIVEN act IS A `s 77 act`
      `the aircraft is in flight` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aircraft is in service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the airport is an airport serving international civil aviation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses a weapon, substance or device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the information to be false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77 the person endangers the safety of an aircraft or airport` MEANS
    IF act EQUALS `s 77 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (g)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one who (a) ... (g)"
    ELSE IF `its paragraph is met`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph's own conditions ("in flight", "in service", "using a weapon", "likely to endanger", "knows to be false")
    WHERE
        `its paragraph is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER act
            WHEN `s 77(a) on board an aircraft in flight, commits an act of violence against a person that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft` THEN `the aircraft is in flight` AND `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names`
            WHEN `s 77(b) using a weapon, commits an act of violence against a person at an airport serving international civil aviation that causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death and that endangers or is likely to endanger safety at the airport` THEN `the person uses a weapon` AND `the airport is an airport serving international civil aviation` AND `the act causes or is likely to cause serious injury or death` AND `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names`
            WHEN `s 77(c) causes damage to an aircraft in service that renders the aircraft incapable of flight or that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft in flight` THEN `the aircraft is in service` AND `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names`
            WHEN `s 77(d) places or causes to be placed on board an aircraft in service anything that is likely to cause damage to the aircraft, that will render it incapable of flight or that is likely to endanger the safety of the aircraft in flight` THEN `the aircraft is in service` AND `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names`
            WHEN `s 77(e) causes damage to or interferes with the operation of any air navigation facility where the damage or interference is likely to endanger the safety of an aircraft in flight` THEN `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names`
            WHEN `s 77(f) using a weapon, substance or device, destroys or causes serious damage to the facilities of an airport serving international civil aviation or to any aircraft not in service located there, or causes disruption of services of the airport, that endangers or is likely to endanger safety at the airport` THEN `the person uses a weapon, substance or device` AND `the airport is an airport serving international civil aviation` AND `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names`
            WHEN `s 77(g) endangers the safety of an aircraft in flight by communicating to any other person any information that the person knows to be false` THEN `the aircraft is in flight` AND `the person knows the information to be false` AND `the act endangers, or is likely to endanger, the safety the paragraph names`
            WHEN `s 77 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (g)` THEN FALSE

@ref Criminal Code s 77 (endangering safety of aircraft or airport) (src:1154-1163)
`s 77 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 77 (endangering safety of aircraft or airport) (src:1154-1163)
`s 77 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 78 -- Offensive weapons and explosive substances on a civil aircraft`

-- Subsection (2): "For the purposes of this section, civil aircraft means all aircraft other than aircraft operated by the Canadian Forces, a police force in Canada or persons engaged in the
-- administration or enforcement of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001." A "means" definition (JUST FALSE outside it). "Canadian Forces" is s 2's term (a seam input).
-- src:1169 | Definition of civil aircraft
-- src:1170 | (2) For the purposes of this section, civil aircraft means all aircraft other than aircraft operated by the Canadian Forces, a police force in Canada or persons engaged in the administration or enforcement of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001.
@ref Criminal Code s 78(2) (definition of civil aircraft) (src:1169-1170)
GIVEN `it is an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 Canadian Forces: the operator is the Canadian Forces` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is operated by a police force in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is operated by persons engaged in the administration or enforcement of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(2) the aircraft is a civil aircraft` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an aircraft` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "civil aircraft means all aircraft"
        IF `s 2 Canadian Forces: the operator is the Canadian Forces` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `it is operated by a police force in Canada` OR `it is operated by persons engaged in the administration or enforcement of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "civil aircraft means all aircraft other than aircraft operated by the Canadian Forces, a police force in Canada or persons engaged in the administration or enforcement of the Customs Act, the Excise Act or the Excise Act, 2001"
        IF `s 2 Canadian Forces: the operator is the Canadian Forces` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 2 "Canadian Forces" leaves the operator open
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (1): "Every one, other than a peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty, who takes on board a civil aircraft an offensive weapon or any explosive substance (a) without the consent of the owner or
-- operator of the aircraft or of a person duly authorized by either of them to consent thereto, or (b) with the consent referred to in paragraph (a) but without complying with all terms and conditions on which the consent
-- was given, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years." "Other than a peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty": read as outside the offence
-- but not the text's own no (NOTHING: fork F12). "Peace officer", "offensive weapon" and "explosive substance" are s 2's terms (seam inputs).
-- src:1164 | Offensive weapons and explosive substances
-- src:1165 | 78 (1) Every one, other than a peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty, who takes on board a civil aircraft an offensive weapon or any explosive substance
-- src:1166 | (a) without the consent of the owner or operator of the aircraft or of a person duly authorized by either of them to consent thereto, or
-- src:1167 | (b) with the consent referred to in paragraph (a) but without complying with all terms and conditions on which the consent was given,
-- src:1168 | is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 78(1) (offensive weapons and explosive substances) (src:1164-1168)
DECLARE `s 78(1) consent position` IS ONE OF
    `s 78(1)(a) without the consent of the owner or operator of the aircraft or of a person duly authorized by either of them to consent thereto`
    `s 78(1)(b) with the consent referred to in paragraph (a) but without complying with all terms and conditions on which the consent was given`
    `s 78(1) with that consent and in compliance with all its terms and conditions`

@ref Criminal Code s 78(1) (offensive weapons and explosive substances) (src:1164-1168)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is a peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is engaged in the execution of the officer's duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 78(2) the aircraft is a civil aircraft: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person takes the thing on board the aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 offensive weapon: the thing is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the consent position` IS A `s 78(1) consent position`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(1) the person takes an offensive weapon or an explosive substance on board a civil aircraft` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2 peace officer: the person is a peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 2 peace officer: the person is a peace officer` EQUALS NOTHING) AND `the peace officer is engaged in the execution of the officer's duty` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than a peace officer engaged in the execution of his duty" (and points outside the text when s 2 "peace officer includes" leaves the person's status open)
        IF `s 78(2) the aircraft is a civil aircraft: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "civil aircraft means all aircraft other than" (subsection (2))
        IF NOT `the person takes the thing on board the aircraft` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who takes on board a civil aircraft"
        IF NOT (`s 2 offensive weapon: the thing is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offensive weapon or any explosive substance" (s 2 leaves the term open when it does not answer JUST TRUE)
        IF `the consent position` EQUALS `s 78(1) with that consent and in compliance with all its terms and conditions` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) without the consent ... or (b) with the consent ... but without complying with all terms and conditions"
        IF `s 78(2) the aircraft is a civil aircraft: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the aircraft is a civil aircraft is left open

@ref Criminal Code s 78(1) (offensive weapons and explosive substances) (src:1164-1168)
`s 78(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 78(1) (offensive weapons and explosive substances) (src:1164-1168)
`s 78(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 78.1 -- Seizing control of ship or fixed platform`

-- Subsection (5): "fixed platform means an artificial island or a marine installation or structure that is permanently attached to the seabed for the purpose of exploration or exploitation of resources or for
-- other economic purposes; ship means every description of vessel not permanently attached to the seabed, other than a warship, a ship being used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes or a ship
-- that has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up." Closed "means" definitions.
-- src:1184 | Definitions
-- src:1185 | (5) In this section,
-- src:1186 | fixed platform means an artificial island or a marine installation or structure that is permanently attached to the seabed for the purpose of exploration or exploitation of resources or for other economic purposes; (plate-forme fixe)
-- src:1187 | ship means every description of vessel not permanently attached to the seabed, other than a warship, a ship being used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes or a ship that has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up. (navire)
@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(5) (definitions) (src:1184-1187)
GIVEN `it is an artificial island or a marine installation or structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is permanently attached to the seabed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of exploration or exploitation of resources or for other economic purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform` MEANS
    IF `it is an artificial island or a marine installation or structure` AND `it is permanently attached to the seabed` AND `it is for the purpose of exploration or exploitation of resources or for other economic purposes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "fixed platform means an artificial island or a marine installation or structure that is permanently attached to the seabed for the purpose of exploration or exploitation of resources or for other economic purposes"

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(5) (definitions) (src:1184-1187)
GIVEN `it is a vessel of any description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is permanently attached to the seabed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a warship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is being used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship` MEANS
    IF `it is a vessel of any description` AND (NOT `it is permanently attached to the seabed`) AND (NOT `it is a warship`) AND (NOT `it is being used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes`) AND (NOT `it has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ship means every description of vessel not permanently attached to the seabed, other than a warship, a ship being used as a naval auxiliary or for customs or police purposes or a ship that has been withdrawn from navigation or is laid up"

-- src:1171 | Seizing control of ship or fixed platform
-- src:1172 | 78.1 (1) Every one who seizes or exercises control over a ship or fixed platform by force or threat of force or by any other form of intimidation is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(1) (seizing control of ship or fixed platform) (src:1171-1172)
GIVEN `the person seizes or exercises control by force or threat of force or by any other form of intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78.1(1) the person seizes control of a ship or fixed platform` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ship means every description of vessel" and "fixed platform means an artificial island" (subsection (5))
        IF `the person seizes or exercises control by force or threat of force or by any other form of intimidation` AND (`s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who seizes or exercises control over a ship or fixed platform by force or threat of force or by any other form of intimidation"

-- src:1173 | Endangering safety of ship or fixed platform
-- src:1174 | (2) Every one who
-- src:1175 | (a) commits an act of violence against a person on board a ship or fixed platform,
-- src:1176 | (b) destroys or causes damage to a ship or its cargo or to a fixed platform,
-- src:1177 | (c) destroys or causes serious damage to or interferes with the operation of any maritime navigational facility, or
-- src:1178 | (d) places or causes to be placed on board a ship or fixed platform anything that is likely to cause damage to the ship or its cargo or to the fixed platform,
-- src:1179 | where that act is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(2) (endangering safety of ship or fixed platform) (src:1173-1179)
DECLARE `s 78.1(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78.1(2)(a) commits an act of violence against a person on board a ship or fixed platform`
    `s 78.1(2)(b) destroys or causes damage to a ship or its cargo or to a fixed platform`
    `s 78.1(2)(c) destroys or causes serious damage to or interferes with the operation of any maritime navigational facility`
    `s 78.1(2)(d) places or causes to be placed on board a ship or fixed platform anything that is likely to cause damage to the ship or its cargo or to the fixed platform`
    `s 78.1(2) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)`

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(2) (endangering safety of ship or fixed platform) (src:1173-1179)
GIVEN act IS A `s 78.1(2) act`
      `s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78.1(2) the person endangers the safety of a ship or fixed platform` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `s 78.1(2) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (d)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one who (a) ... (d)"
        IF NOT `the act is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where that act is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform"
        IF act EQUALS `s 78.1(2)(c) destroys or causes serious damage to or interferes with the operation of any maritime navigational facility` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 78.1(5) the thing is a ship: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 78.1(5) the thing is a fixed platform: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a ship or fixed platform"

-- src:1180 | False communication
-- src:1181 | (3) Every one who communicates information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship, knowing the information to be false, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(3) (false communication) (src:1180-1181)
GIVEN `the person communicates information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the information to be false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78.1(3) the person communicates false information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship` MEANS
    IF `the person communicates information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship` AND `the person knows the information to be false`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who communicates information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship, knowing the information to be false"

-- src:1182 | Threats causing death or injury
-- src:1183 | (4) Every one who threatens to commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a), (b) or (c) in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing any act, where the threat is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(4) (threats causing death or injury) (src:1182-1183)
DECLARE `s 78.1(4) threatened offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 78.1(4) an offence under paragraph (2)(a)`
    `s 78.1(4) an offence under paragraph (2)(b)`
    `s 78.1(4) an offence under paragraph (2)(c)`
    `s 78.1(4) an offence under paragraph (2)(d)`
    `s 78.1(4) an offence under another provision`

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(4) (threats causing death or injury) (src:1182-1183)
GIVEN `the person threatens` IS A BOOLEAN
      threatened IS A `s 78.1(4) threatened offence`
      `the threat is in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing any act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the threat is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78.1(4) the person threatens to commit an offence under paragraph 78.1(2)(a), (b) or (c)` MEANS
    IF `the person threatens`
        AND (threatened EQUALS `s 78.1(4) an offence under paragraph (2)(a)` OR threatened EQUALS `s 78.1(4) an offence under paragraph (2)(b)` OR threatened EQUALS `s 78.1(4) an offence under paragraph (2)(c)`)
        AND `the threat is in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing any act`
        AND `the threat is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who threatens to commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a), (b) or (c) in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing any act, where the threat is likely to endanger"

-- Every offence in section 78.1 is "guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life".
-- src:1171 | Seizing control of ship or fixed platform
-- src:1172 | 78.1 (1) Every one who seizes or exercises control over a ship or fixed platform by force or threat of force or by any other form of intimidation is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
-- src:1173 | Endangering safety of ship or fixed platform
-- src:1174 | (2) Every one who
-- src:1175 | (a) commits an act of violence against a person on board a ship or fixed platform,
-- src:1176 | (b) destroys or causes damage to a ship or its cargo or to a fixed platform,
-- src:1177 | (c) destroys or causes serious damage to or interferes with the operation of any maritime navigational facility, or
-- src:1178 | (d) places or causes to be placed on board a ship or fixed platform anything that is likely to cause damage to the ship or its cargo or to the fixed platform,
-- src:1179 | where that act is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
-- src:1180 | False communication
-- src:1181 | (3) Every one who communicates information that endangers the safe navigation of a ship, knowing the information to be false, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
-- src:1182 | Threats causing death or injury
-- src:1183 | (4) Every one who threatens to commit an offence under paragraph (2)(a), (b) or (c) in order to compel a person to do or refrain from doing any act, where the threat is likely to endanger the safe navigation of a ship or the safety of a fixed platform, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(1) to (4) (punishment) (src:1171-1183)
`s 78.1 the class of the offences in subsections (1) to (4)` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 78.1(1) to (4) (punishment) (src:1171-1183)
`s 78.1 the punishment for the offences in subsections (1) to (4)` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
